# The corpus is addressed by character offset. Every requirement span, every
# section lookup and every offset-map test is stated in raw character positions
# into these files.
#
# core.autocrlf is on by default on Windows installs, so without this rule git
# would check the corpus out with CRLF on Windows and LF on Linux CI. That shifts
# every raw offset by one per preceding line — tests pass on one platform and
# fail on the other, and the offset map gets blamed for a git problem.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion: the bytes on disk are the bytes in
# the object store, on every platform.
corpus/** -text
